// `EVERPARSE_COPY_BUFFER_T` is an abstract, input-stream-independent handle in
// both backends, so merely *mentioning* it -- as a type parameter, or as the
// parameter of an `extern` action -- must work with every `--input_stream`
// binding.
//
// Under `--api pulse` it used to be printed as `B.copy_buffer_t`, where `B` is the
// input-stream module alias. Only `EverParse3d.InputStream.Buffer` re-exports
// that name (from `EverParse3d.CopyBuffer.Buffer`), so on `extern` and
// `static` the frontend accepted this file and F* then failed on the generated
// code with
//
//   Error 72: Identifier copy_buffer_t not found in module B
//
// That is why this test is `--batch` rather than generation-only: the
// regression is invisible to the frontend.
//
// Note there is no `probe` here. Probing *is* buffer-only under `--api pulse`;
// that restriction is pinned by the negative half of this test.

extern void Save(EVERPARSE_COPY_BUFFER_T dest, UINT32 x)

entrypoint
typedef struct _withCopyBuffer (EVERPARSE_COPY_BUFFER_T dest)
{
  UINT32 x {:on-success Save(dest, x); return true; };
} withCopyBuffer;
